        <section id="the-key-points-of-legislation-and-guidance"  class="t-bg-primary">
          
            <h2>The key points of legislation and guidance</h2>
              <p>Let’s look at the key points of legislation and how they relate to autism in the following slides.</p>

              
              
<div class="gallery-container">
  <div role="group" class="gallery no-js">
    <ul>
        <li role="listitem">
          
    <div class="l-media ">
        
        <h2 class="l-media__title">
          Autism Act
        </h2>

      <div class="l-media__body ">
        <p>The Autism Act of 2009 makes provision for the needs of adults on the autism spectrum and is the first ever disability specific legislation to be passed in the UK. It has brought about changes in the way those with autism access support.</p>

      </div>
          <img class="l-media__img" src="~/images/svg/demo/ua_u2_s1_p2_slide1.svg" alt="" width="300" height="300" >  
    </div>
        </li>
        <li role="listitem">
          
    <div class="l-media ">
        
        <h2 class="l-media__title">
          Equality Act
        </h2>

      <div class="l-media__body ">
        <p>The Equality Act of 2010 combined previous anti-discrimination laws into one. It provides a legal framework to protect the rights of individuals and promote equal opportunities for everyone. It makes clear what public, private and voluntary sectors must legally do to ensure that people with protected characteristics such as a learning disability are not disadvantaged.</p>

      </div>
          <img class="l-media__img" src="~/images/svg/demo/ua_u2_s1_p2_slide2.svg" alt="" width="300" height="300" >  
    </div>
        </li>
        <li role="listitem">
          
    <div class="l-media ">
        
        <h2 class="l-media__title">
          Mental Capacity Act
        </h2>

      <div class="l-media__body ">
        <p>The Mental Capacity Act of 2005 (MCA) provides a framework to protect people who may lack capacity to make some decisions for themselves. To be able to make a decision, a person has to be able to understand and retain the relevant information. Individuals can have a ‘capacity assessment’ the purpose which is not to judge the decision a person makes but is to determine whether a person is able to make the decision.</p>

      </div>
          <img class="l-media__img" src="~/images/svg/demo/ua_u2_s1_p2_slide3.svg" alt="" width="300" height="300" >  
    </div>
        </li>
        <li role="listitem">
          
    <div class="l-media ">
        
        <h2 class="l-media__title">
          Human Rights Act
        </h2>

      <div class="l-media__body ">
        <p>The Human Rights Act of 1998 sets out the fundamental rights and freedoms that everyone in the UK is entitled to. The Act requires all public authorities such as government departments, councils, hospitals, the police etc to act in a way which respects and protects an individual’s human rights, regardless of whether they have a learning disability or not.</p>

      </div>
          <img class="l-media__img" src="~/images/svg/demo/ua_u2_s1_p2_slide4.svg" alt="" width="300" height="300" >  
    </div>
        </li>
        <li role="listitem">
          
    <div class="l-media ">
        
        <h2 class="l-media__title">
          ‘Fulfilling and Rewarding Lives’ and ‘Think Autism’
        </h2>

      <div class="l-media__body ">
        <p>In 2010 the Government set out a strategy with a built in reviews for meeting the needs of adults on the autism spectrum by improving the provision of services by local authorities and the NHS. This strategy ‘Fulfilling and Rewarding Lives’ aimed to improve outcomes for adults with autism and was updated with ‘Think autism’ in 2014 and called for a society and cultural shift so that equality and human rights of those with autism are respected.</p>

      </div>
          <img class="l-media__img" src="~/images/svg/demo/ua_u2_s1_p2_slide5.svg" alt="" width="300" height="300" >  
    </div>
        </li>
        <li role="listitem">
          
    <div class="l-media ">
        
        <h2 class="l-media__title">
          Care Act
        </h2>

      <div class="l-media__body ">
        <p>The Care Act 2014 as well as expanding on previous guidance from 2010 expands on the responsibilities of local authorities and the NHS, for example, giving guidance on the different levels of training, preventative support and safeguarding, equality, supporting people with autism and complex needs, employment and criminal justice.</p>

      </div>
          <img class="l-media__img" src="~/images/svg/demo/ua_u2_s1_p2_slide6.svg" alt="" width="300" height="300" >  
    </div>
        </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</div>

            
          
        </section>
        
    
     
    
  
     
    
  
  
